Logic :

Traverse the array only once while maintaining the current prefix sum. 
At every index, calculate the remainder of the current prefix sum when divided by k. 
If the same remainder has already appeared before, then the subarray between the previous prefix sum and the current prefix sum is divisible by k,
because equal remainders imply their difference is a multiple of k.
Since the same remainder can occur multiple times, store its frequency in a HashMap and add that frequency to the answer. 
If the remainder is negative, convert it to a positive remainder by adding k, so all equivalent remainders are treated the same.
Finally,  store the current remainder in the map and continue traversing the array.

Code :

class Solution {
    public int subarraysDivByK(int[] nums, int k) {
        int prefix=0;
        int c=0;
        HashMap<Integer,Integer> map=new HashMap<>();
        map.put(0,1);
        for(int num:nums){
            prefix+=num;
            int rem=prefix%k;
            if(rem<0){
                rem+=k;
            }
             c+=map.getOrDefault(rem,0);
            map.put(rem,map.getOrDefault(rem,0)+1);
        }
        return c;
    }
}
